## 🧭 Project Overview

This is a full-stack real-time multiplayer board game (Richup.io clone).
- **Frontend:** React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion, React Router v6
- **Backend:** Django 5, Django Channels 4, Django REST Framework, PostgreSQL, Redis
- **Protocol:** REST for lobby/auth, WebSocket (JSON messages) for live game state
- **The backend is the single source of truth for ALL game state.**

---

## 📁 File & Folder Conventions

### Frontend (`frontend/src/`)
- `pages/` — Top-level route components only. No business logic. Keep them thin.
- `components/ui/` — shadcn/ui primitives. Do not modify these directly.
- `components/game/` — Game-specific presentational components (board, tile, token, dice).
- `components/lobby/` — Lobby and room management components.
- `hooks/` — Custom React hooks. One hook per file. Named `use<Feature>.ts`.
- `store/` — Zustand stores. One store per domain. Named `use<Domain>Store.ts`.
- `types/` — TypeScript interfaces and enums shared across the frontend. No logic here.
- `lib/` — Pure utility functions. Must be side-effect free and unit testable.
- `routes/` — React Router configuration only.

### Backend (`backend/`)
- `config/` — Django project settings, urls, asgi, wsgi. No app logic here.
- `apps/<app>/` — Each Django app is a focused domain: `rooms`, `game`, `accounts`.
  - `models.py` — Django ORM models. Keep methods small.
  - `views.py` — DRF views / viewsets for REST endpoints.
  - `consumers.py` — Django Channels WebSocket consumers.
  - `serializers.py` — DRF serializers. Validate ALL input here.
  - `routing.py` — WebSocket URL routing for the app.
  - `urls.py` — REST URL routing for the app.
  - `services.py` — Business logic layer. Views/consumers call services, not models directly.
  - `tests/` — Tests mirroring the app structure.

