## 🔤 Naming Conventions

### TypeScript / React
- Components: `PascalCase` (`GameBoard`, `PlayerToken`, `DiceRoller`)
- Hooks: `camelCase` prefixed with `use` (`useWebSocket`, `useGameState`)
- Zustand stores: `camelCase` prefixed with `use`, suffixed with `Store` (`useGameStore`)
- Types / Interfaces: `PascalCase`, no `I` prefix (`GameState`, `Player`, `Tile`)
- Enums: `PascalCase` name, `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` values (`TileType.GO_TO_JAIL`)
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` in dedicated `constants.ts` files
- Event handlers: prefix with `handle` (`handleRollDice`, `handleBuyProperty`)
- Boolean variables/props: prefix with `is`, `has`, `can` (`isMyTurn`, `hasJailCard`)

### Python / Django
- Models: `PascalCase`, singular (`Room`, `GameState`, `Player`)
- Views / Consumers: `PascalCase` with suffix (`RoomListView`, `GameConsumer`)
- Serializers: `PascalCase` with `Serializer` suffix (`RoomSerializer`)
- Services: `snake_case` functions in `services.py` (`create_room`, `process_roll`)
- URL names: `kebab-case` (`room-list`, `room-detail`)
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` in `constants.py`
- Test files: `test_<module>.py` (`test_views.py`, `test_consumers.py`, `test_services.py`)

