## ⚠️ Things to Never Do

- ❌ Never trust client-sent `player_id` — always derive it from the authenticated session/token.
- ❌ Never store game state only in memory (Django process restarts will wipe it) — persist to Redis or DB.
- ❌ Never put secrets in code or version control.
- ❌ Never use `any` in TypeScript.
- ❌ Never perform game actions inside React components — dispatch WS messages and let the server respond.
- ❌ Never write business logic in Django views — use the services layer.
- ❌ Never expose stack traces to API clients in production.
- ❌ Never skip serializer validation in consumers or views.
- ❌ Never block the async event loop in Django Channels consumers (no synchronous DB calls — use `database_sync_to_async`).

```python
# ✅ Correct async DB access in consumers
from channels.db import database_sync_to_async

class GameConsumer(AsyncJsonWebsocketConsumer):
    async def handle_buy_property(self, content):
        room = await database_sync_to_async(Room.objects.get)(code=self.room_code)
        # ...
```
